        "raw": "<p>Although I&#39;ve been playing SotM for years, I still consider myself a noob. &nbsp;Yesterday I decided to try advanced mode for the first time and figured I&#39;d wade in against Baron Blade for nostalgic reasons. &nbsp;What ensued was an embarassing beatdown of BB that I had to share:</p><p>Basically, we fought in the Ruins of Atlantis. &nbsp;I don&#39;t even remember who all the heroes were because it really came down to Visionary and Legacy. &nbsp;Pillars of Hercules came out and I managed to hold out against all the extra villain plays until Legacy&#39;s turn. &nbsp;I had two Takedowns in hand, plus Next Evolution. &nbsp;I played Takedown, used Galvanize and Next Evolution to make myself immune to the energy damage that BB would deal me for playing Takedown. &nbsp;For a full round I got an extra power, play, and draw with no drawback because BB couldn&#39;t play cards. &nbsp;One Takedown left play and I played the other and used the same two powers as I described above. &nbsp;On Visionary&#39;s turn, I used Mental Divergence to put Takedown from the trash back on top of Legacy&#39;s deck. &nbsp;Lather, rinse, repeat.</p><p>For four or five turns, I kept Pillars of Hercules in play while I pounded on Baron Blade. &nbsp;At one point I actually debated stopping the combo because I had absolutely zero risk of losing, but I decided to see it through to the end.</p>",
